WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.537
The first step with missing data is usually to count it.

00:00:03.537 --> 00:00:08.267
Isna dot sum tells us how many missing values appear in each column.

00:00:08.267 --> 00:00:14.102
Here channel has one missing value and amount has one missing value.

00:00:14.102 --> 00:00:19.992
The example fills the missing channel with “unknown” and replaces the missing amount with the median of the available

00:00:19.992 --> 00:00:22.009
amounts.

00:00:22.459 --> 00:00:26.021
Those are example decisions, not universal rules.

00:00:26.021 --> 00:00:32.840
In a real project, the correct treatment depends on why the data is missing and how the field will be used.
